      "text": [
        " قَالَ أَمِيرُ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ ( عليه السلام ) إِيَّاكُمْ وَ نِكَاحَ الزِّنْجِ فَإِنَّهُ خَلْقٌ مُشَوَّهٌ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from Haroun Bin Muslim, from Mas’ada Bin Ziyad, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘Amir Al-Momineen<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘Beware of marrying (the people of) <span class=\"iTxt\">Al-Zanj</span>, (a coastal region of Africa) for these are disfigured creatures’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "1. Ali has narrated from Harun ibn Muslim from Mas’adah ibn Ziyad who has said the following: “Abu ‘ Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said that ’Amir al-Mu’minin has said, ’You must remain on your guard against marriage with people of al-Zanj because it is a distorted creature.’” "
        ]
      }
